  "body": "Offered to the market for the first time in nearly three decades, this central Takapuna property is being sold as a deceased estate with clear instructions from the executors - this property MUST BE SOLD. \r\n\r\nTo reflect its 1998 plaster exterior and unconsented historical work, pricing expectations are grounded firmly in market reality.\r\n\r\nThe Key Fundamentals:\r\n\r\n* Deceased Estate: Tightly held for 28 years with motivated executors seeking a transparent, clean outcome.\r\n\r\n* Significant Project Scope: Original plaster construction sold \"as-is, where-is\"-the perfect canvas to reclad, remodel, remediate, or land-bank in a blue-chip zone.\r\n\r\n* Substantial 2-Level Footprint: Features 3 well-proportioned bedrooms, 2 bathrooms, light-filled living zones, double garaging, and a private sheltered pergola retreat. \r\n\r\n* Coveted Central Address: An easy walk to Takapuna Beach, tranquil Lake Pupuke, vibrant artisan cafes, dining, and Shore City, alongside top-tier school zoning and rapid SH1 motorway access.\r\n\r\nOpportunities offering this degree of location and value-add scale are exceedingly rare. For reclad specialists, builders, visionary renovators, and strategic land-bankers, the fundamentals here are undeniable. You are securing a generous footprint on a low-maintenance section in a premier central Takapuna pocket-leaving all the future capital upside entirely in your hands.\r\n\r\nThe executors are committed to achieving a sale. Ignore the CV, bring your builder, complete your due diligence and explore this opportunity in one of Takapuna's most tightly held pockets.\r\n\r\nContact Rohit to arrange an inspection and obtain the full disclosure documentation.\r\n\r\nAuction: 2:00pm, Thursday 19 November 2026 at 3 Pompallier Terrace, Ponsonby (Unless Sold Prior)",
